    }
    assert frequency_lists([]) == {}
    print("All tests passed!")
```

The function loops over every element in every sublist and counts each one in a dictionary. `freq.get(item, 0) + 1` increments the count and starts new elements at 0. Python dictionaries keep insertion order, so keys appear in the order they are first seen.

